# .pubignore REPLACES .gitignore for `dart pub publish`.
#
# It exists so the DevTools extension bundle SHIPS. The root .gitignore
# excludes every `build/` directory (canvaskit has no business in git history
# twice over — leonard_flutter already tracks a copy for consumer
# auto-discovery), but pub archives git-tracked files by default, so the panel
# bundle was simply absent from the archive and pub rejected the package:
#
#   It looks like you are making a devtools extension!
#   The folder `extension/devtools` should contain both a `config.yaml` file
#   and a non-empty `build` directory
#
# Because this file takes precedence over .gitignore, the build/ directory is
# included in the published archive while staying untracked in git. The
# publish workflow runs tool/build_devtools_extension.sh before publishing, so
# the shipped bundle is built from the tagged source — it is a build artifact,
# never a source of truth.
#
# Everything below mirrors the root .gitignore EXCEPT the devtools build.
.dart_tool/
build/
!extension/devtools/build/
.packages
pubspec.lock
